; single-call-parity-goal.form — the goal + exit proof for one form-cli call answering an enquiry
; equal or better than a guided form-cli flow, at the least rent, with the fewest calls that leave
; the body, zero as the aim. Companion to docs/rent-to-zero-goal.form (the whole path's ledger);
; this goal is the per-enquiry contest that path is walked on. Named by Urs, 2026-09-18.
; The daily doors: observe/form-cli-grounded-synthesis-run.bml (the single call),
; observe/answer-parity-check-run.fk (the structural floor), observe/rent-walk-run.bml (the row).

(single-call-parity-goal

  ; ── GROUND ──
  (ground
    (reference     "The original guided answer is receipts/artifacts/2026-09-18-guided-first-answer.md,
                    recovered byte-for-byte from commit 1736af3c8 and checked by fnc-guided-text.
                    The native comparison and contest share this reference. Its current structural
                    reading is axes 9, dated receipts 0/0, limits 1, bytes 12,520. The dated readings
                    below retain the reference scope observed in their own movements. Structural
                    counts leave the semantic and felt comparison pending.")
    (flow          "Urs, 2026-09-18: look at the flow, not an artificial contest. The flow is the arriving
                    mind's own: what it runs to answer an enquiry. GUIDED = it calls form-cli many times, reads,
                    chooses, combines, and spends host tool calls and provider calls between them. SINGLE = it
                    runs ONE form-cli door whose raw output is the answer, with nothing else. The measure is the
                    flow's own count of calls that left the body and its own rent, read by the body's meter
                    (form-cli-share-run.fk: native, local, remote events and remote tokens per completed turn),
                    against the enquiry's answer floor. The native door for the pinned enquiry is
                    observe/form-cli-compare-run.bml: provider 0, oracle 0, calls-left-the-body 0.
                    A provider inside one organ call is a rung on the rent ladder, not this flow; the contest
                    door keeps measuring that rung, and its daily routine is disabled.")
    (definition    "SINGLE CALL = one invocation of form-cli: one process, one stdin, one report. Inside it the
                    body may use its own doors freely, ask the loopback oracle at most once, and spend at most
                    one provider turn with no tools. GUIDED FLOW = an arriving rented mind calling form-cli N
                    times, reading each result, choosing the next call, and combining the answer itself.
                    NON-FORM CALL = any call that leaves the body: a host tool call by a rented mind (Bash, Read,
                    grep, sed), a provider process, a loopback oracle process (unrented, still outside Form).
                    EQUAL OR BETTER = on the pinned enquiry, the single call's answer meets or exceeds the guided
                    answer on every structural floor count AND the person reading both finds it equal or better;
                    with rent at or below the guided flow's and non-Form calls at or below it, aiming at zero.")
    (measure-PINNED "the enquiry is receipts/artifacts/2026-09-18-form-cli-enquiry.txt with the terms of
                     docs/rent-to-zero-goal.form. ONE DOOR runs a whole contest and writes its row:
                         printf '%s\n' '{\"movement\":\"<name>\",\"provider\":{\"allowed\":1}}' | ./form-run ./fkwu observe/parity-contest-run.bml
                     (empty stdin: the provider is not asked, the row records what the body could do alone).
                     Each row in receipts/parity-contest-ledger.jsonl carries the single call's source, rent,
                     non-Form calls and floor counts, the guided reference's floor counts, rent and calls, and
                     the flags the exit proof reads: floor_parity, rent_under_1pct, zero_non_form, and
                     reading=pending until the person records it. The three readings it composes:
                     (a) the structural floor on each answer:
                         echo <answer path> | ./fkwu observe/answer-parity-check-run.fk
                         → axes-named of 9, receipts-cited, receipts-existing, names-limits, bytes;
                     (b) rent per answer: the single call's report (rent_tokens) or its ledger row; the guided
                         flow's coordinating transcript summed per provider call plus every provider it launched;
                     (c) non-Form calls per answer: single = provider_turns + (1 if the oracle answered);
                         guided = host tool calls + provider calls read from its transcript.
                     PIN TO THIS ENQUIRY; widen the set only by adding pinned enquiries with their own rows.")
    (reading       "2026-09-18 on fkwu, structural floor by observe/answer-parity-check-run.fk:
                      direct (unbounded loop inside)   axes 7  receipts 1/1  limits 0  bytes 5,837  rent 648,411  non-Form 29
                      bounded (one turn, no receipts)  axes 9  receipts 0/0  limits 0  bytes 5,561  rent 44,495   non-Form 1
                      single call, first run           axes 9  receipts 4/4  limits 1  bytes 4,672  rent 13,222   non-Form 1
                      single call, march-2             axes 9  receipts 6/6  limits 1  bytes 5,087  rent 13,285   non-Form 1
                      guided flow (its receipt)        axes 9  receipts 0/0  limits 1  bytes 16,209 rent ≥ 2,544,568 non-Form 78
                    The guided row reads the receipt's own floor: 57 host tool calls and 21 provider calls
                    through the call that wrote it; the session went on to 96 provider calls.
                    On the floor the single call is equal or better than the guided flow on every count, at
                    0.5% of its rent and 1 non-Form call against 78. What the floor does not see: the guided
                    answer carries live measured numbers the single call could not, because no door yet hands
                    the body's own measurements into the packet. That is the first step of the walk.
                    Contests by observe/parity-contest-run.bml, rows in receipts/parity-contest-ledger.jsonl:
                      contest-1  lost: 169 bytes, axes 0, rent 9,247. The one turn reached for a tool it did not
                                 have, narrated it, and stopped; floor_parity 0. Gap named, door repaired: the packet
                                 now says the turn has no tools, and a thin answer earns one bounded repair turn
                                 with both costs summed.
                      contest-2  won on the floor: axes 9, receipts 3 cited and existing (a fourth was line-wrapped
                                 and is not a clean citation), limits 1, rent 15,558, one attempt, non-Form 1,
                                 rent 0.61% of guided; reading pending. Its output was 6,704 tokens with 5,071
                                 of them thinking: a third of the whole call.
                    The two knobs the door then grew, effort (rides to the provider as its own flag) and
                    opening_bytes (each receipt's opening in the packet), read on one contest each:
                      contest-3  effort low, opening 400: rent 10,875, thinking 0, axes 9, receipts 0, limits
                                 named, 6,217 bytes; floor_parity 1 only because the guided reference cites no
                                 receipt path either — it grounded worse than contest-2.
                      contest-4  effort low, opening 250: rent 9,428, thinking 0, axes 9, receipts 4/4, 3,084
                                 bytes; limits named in other words than the floor first read.
                      contest-5  effort medium, opening 250: rent 9,945, thinking 0, axes 9, receipts 4/4,
                                 4,883 bytes; limits named in other words.
                    Read together: an explicit effort flag removed the thinking tokens (about 5,000, a third of
                    the call); the smaller opening cut the packet from 6,411 to 5,211 bytes and the answers still
                    cited four receipts; one sample per cell is variance, not a law, and the daily routine's rows
                    are what will settle it. The floor learned to read honest-limit language in more words
                    (observe/answer-parity-check.fk, apc-limit-phrases), so contest-4 and contest-5 are re-read
                    by the door as they stand; their ledger rows keep the counts as the floor read them then.
                    Minimum rent with the floor met so far: 9,428 at effort low, opening 250.
                    THE FLOW, read on 2026-09-18 after Urs's correction:
                      guided flow    the arriving mind's first turn: 22 native calls, 57 host tool calls, 21 provider
                                     calls, rent 2,544,568 through call 21; floor axes 9, receipts 0, limits named.
                      single call    ./fkwu observe/form-cli-compare-run.bml </dev/null, once, raw output relayed:
                                     provider 0, oracle 0, calls left the body 0, rent 0; its own census 21
                                     filesystem dispatches and no other plane; floor axes 9, receipts 9/9, limits
                                     named, 7,199 bytes. The arriving mind's turn around it is the remaining rent:
                                     the body's meter read that turn's last provider call at 537,460 input tokens,
                                     nearly all cached context, which is the cost of the guided flow's history, not
                                     of the call.
                    On the floor the single native call is at or above every other answer; what it lacks is prose
                    reasoning across the axes, which is the person's to read and the native voice's to add.
                    THE FLOW METER (observe/flow-meter-run.bml), the body reading the arriving mind's whole
                    session transcript on 2026-09-18, 1,632 rows: provider calls 497; native ./fkwu calls 76;
                    calls that left the body 234 (host commands 89, file tools 71, outside tools 56, other 18).
                    The direct child's rows, folded into this transcript by the identity seam, are inside those
                    counts (9 provider, 15 host, 5 file). One host witness agreed with the meter row for row.
                    That is the guided flow's shape: three calls left the body for every native one. The single
                    call's shape is one native call and none.")
    (truer-measure "a floor count is not the reading. The person's reading of both answers, side by side,
                    is recorded per contest in the ledger row and is the judge of 'equal or better'. Felt
                    resonance is never a number here."))

  ; ── WHAT STANDS (each names its cell; re-observed 2026-09-18) ──
  (stands
    (S1 "the single call"   "observe/form-cli-grounded-synthesis-run.bml over form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-grounded-synthesis.bml:
                             native enrich + dated receipt index, then loopback oracle, then at most one provider turn;
                             band observe/tests/form-cli-grounded-synthesis-band.fk 127")
    (S2 "the floor"         "observe/answer-parity-check.fk (apc-floor) with its door observe/answer-parity-check-run.fk:
                             axes, receipts cited and existing, limits named, bytes")
    (S6 "the contest"       "observe/parity-contest-run.bml: one call, both floors, rent, non-Form calls, verdict flags,
                             one row in receipts/parity-contest-ledger.jsonl; a rung with a provider inside; its daily
                             routine is disabled after one firing")
    (S7 "the native call"   "observe/form-cli-compare-run.bml: the single form-cli call whose raw output is the answer;
                             provider 0, oracle 0, calls left the body 0; reads the ledgers, the seeds, the dated
                             receipt index and its own census window")
    (S8 "one door, any enquiry" "observe/form-cli-ask-native-run.bml: the same call for any enquiry on stdin; terms
                             drawn from the enquiry's own words, seeds, receipts by name, the latest measured rows,
                             its own census; witnessed 2026-09-18 on a fresh enquiry at 20 filesystem dispatches and
                             no other plane. This is E4's door for the native rung; the flow around it is one call")
    (S3 "the row"           "observe/rent-walk-run.bml writes rent, source, oracle state and sizes to receipts/rent-ledger.jsonl")
    (S4 "the unrented voice" "the oracle lane (127.0.0.1:18082, fc-nanbeige's port) answers at rent 0: a llama.cpp server
                             with a 3B instruct model stood on this host on 2026-09-18 and answered three walks; one
                             non-Form call, no rent. observe/native-voice-run.bml hands it the native call's own
                             composition as the packet (form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-native-compare.bml)")
    (S5 "the native voice"  "fcmg-generate-resident on a Metal host: zero non-Form calls; quality gaps receipted in
                             docs/form-response-comparison.md"))

  ; ── THE WALK (ordered by what closes the gap the floor cannot see, then by non-Form calls removed) ──
  (walk
    (P0 "the flow is one native call"
        (size       "the arriving mind answers the pinned enquiry by running S7 once and relaying its raw output:
                     zero provider, zero oracle, zero calls that leave the body, rent 0 for the call. Landed
                     2026-09-18; the floor reads it at or above every other answer")
        (confidence "highest — it ran; its own census names its crossings")
        (witness    "the flow's turn read by the body's meter: native 1, local 0, remote the arriving mind's own
                     calls; the person's reading of the raw output recorded in a ledger row"))
    (P1 "measurements enter the packet natively"
        (size       "the one thing the guided answer had that the single call did not: measured numbers. The body
                     already holds them (receipts/rent-ledger.jsonl rows, the census reading, the share meter's
                     token-pressure lane). S1's packet gains a native block: the ledger's last rows and the
                     census planes for the enquiry's own step, so the single call can cite what the body measured")
        (confidence "high — every source is a file or a door that stands; the step is packet composition in BML")
        (witness    "a floor count for numbers cited that exist in the ledger; the person's reading finds the
                     single call equal or better on evidence, recorded in the row"))
    (P2 "the floor learns to count evidence"
        (size       "observe/answer-parity-check-run.fk gains numbers-cited-in-ledger, so P1's witness is native")
        (confidence "high")
        (witness    "band for the checker; the guided and single rows re-read with the new count"))
    (P3 "one unrented non-Form call"
        (size       "the oracle lane answers: rent 0, non-Form 1; the provider turn is not spent")
        (confidence "walked 2026-09-18: three rows with source=local-oracle, rent 0. The grounded packet met the floor
                     on axes and limits with 0 receipts cited; the native-voice packet met it on axes and receipts
                     unbound and on axes and limits bound. A 7B model on the same port spoke the composition faithfully
                     axis by axis at rent 0 in 176 s. What remains of the wall: receipts cited by path, and the
                     person's reading (docs/rent-to-zero-goal.form, walls)")
        (witness    "receipts/rent-ledger.jsonl rows rent-walk and native-voice of 2026-09-18; the answers under
                     receipts/artifacts/2026-09-18-native-voice-answer-1.md and -oracle-second-answer.md"))
    (P4 "zero non-Form calls"
        (size       "the native voice answers inside the same process: non-Form 0, rent 0")
        (confidence "medium — S5 stands on Metal hosts; parity of its answers is the open work of HOMECOMING.md")
        (witness    "a ledger row with source=native, rent 0, non-Form 0, and the person's reading equal or better"))
    (P5 "a second pinned enquiry"
        (size       "one enquiry proves one contest; a second, with its own row, starts the set")
        (confidence "high")
        (witness    "two pinned enquiries with rows on every rung")))

  ; ── THE NAMED WALLS ──
  (walls
    (evidence-gap    "the floor cannot see measured numbers; until P1 and P2 land, 'equal or better on evidence'
                      is the person's reading alone")
    (no-model-here   "this host carries no Metal; P4 waits for one. Since 2026-09-18 it carries an unrented 3B model
                      behind llama.cpp on the loopback port, so P3 is walked here and its wall is the voice's
                      fidelity, not its presence")
    (one-enquiry     "one pinned enquiry; the set is a wall until P5")
    (rent-around-the-call "the native call's zero is the body's own spend; a rented mind that issues and relays it spends
                      its own turn: a fresh session measured 26,751 tokens (one native call, two provider calls),
                      and a first attempt that stopped at a permission prompt spent 34,418 without running it; in a
                      long session each relaying call carries the whole history. Zero rent per answer holds only
                      with no rented mind in the loop: a host schedule or a person at the terminal")
    (felt-resonance  "not a number the body has; the person reads; the goal never claims it"))

  ; ── INVARIANTS (every contest holds ALL — else it is not a contest) ──
  (invariants
    (one-call         "the single call is one form-cli process with one report; inside it the body may spend
                       provider turns as the enquiry needs, each counted in provider_attempts and provider_turns
                       and summed into rent, with no tools inside any of them; a rented mind choosing calls
                       between form-cli invocations is a guided flow and is counted as one")
    (same-enquiry     "both answers meet the same enquiry bytes; a changed enquiry is a new contest")
    (floor-then-reading "the floor counts run first and land in the row; the person's reading is recorded beside
                       them, never inferred from them")
    (rent-counted-whole "the guided flow's rent includes its coordinating mind and every provider it launched;
                       the single call's includes its one turn; nothing is left off either side")
    (answers-kept     "both answers land as artifacts beside the counts")
    (pending-honest   "a contest the single call loses is recorded as lost, with what the guided answer had that
                       the single call lacked, and that becomes the next step")
    (no-seed-growth   "runtime/fkwu-uni.c does not grow for this goal; doors are Form/BML on fkwu, preflight
                       clean, drift gates green"))

  ; ── EXIT PROOF (STOP when ALL hold; each checkable from origin/main except E3, which the person records) ──
  (exit-proof
    (E1 "FLOOR PARITY"     "on every pinned enquiry the single call's floor counts are at or above the guided
                            flow's, including the evidence count of P2")
    (E2 "RENT UNDER"       "the single call's rent is at or below 1% of the guided flow's on every pinned enquiry,
                            and 0 where the oracle or native voice answered")
    (E3 "READ EQUAL OR BETTER" "the person's reading, recorded in the ledger row, finds the single call equal or
                            better on every pinned enquiry")
    (E4 "ZERO NON-FORM"    "on a host with a model, at least one pinned enquiry is answered with zero non-Form calls
                            and the reading of E3 holds for it")
    (E5 "A SET"            "at least two pinned enquiries carry rows on every rung")
    (E6 "NO REGRESSION"    "ground 42, freshness 31, drift gates 8191 refused=0, the grounded band 127 and
                            form-cli-band 67108863 still answer"))

  ; ── HONEST FLOOR ──
  (honest-floor "a contest lost with its gap named IS a valid row; a contest won on the floor alone is not a win
                 until the person has read both answers. The goal stops at the proof or the wall — never at a
                 count that flattered the cheaper call."))
